Varun can do a piece of work in 28 days. Waseem is 75% more efficient than Varun. Yash is twice as efficient than Waseem. Varun started the work alone and worked for some days and left the work then Waseem and Yash joined together and completed the work in 4 days. Then how many days does Varun worked alone?
5 days
9 days
10 days
7 days
Solution :

Waseem = 75% more efficient → 1 + 0.75 = 1.75 units
Yash = twice Waseem → 2 × 1.75 = 3.5 units
So daily work units:
Varun = 1
Waseem = 1.75
Yash = 3.5
